(379556, 31807, 5475, '<td valign="top">Must be Kollin...  possibly?<br/>Nice shot of the Lincoln Memorial.  Most shots that you see are close ups...  I like the way this shows more of the architecture.  Great columns, and I love those stairs, even though you can''t see them here.  I''ve taken some night shots here as well...   The lighting creates such a brownish yellow cast.  I would prefer this with a little less yellow... maybe desaturate a little in editing.    I also like that you included some of the lighted wall above the top facade.  I never did this in any of my photos.  Overall, great shot, a place I'' enjoy very much!  8 from me.<br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'Must be Kollin...  possibly?Nice shot of the Lincoln Memorial.  Most shots that you see are close ups...  I like the way this shows more of the architecture.  Great columns, and I love those stairs, even though you can''t see them here.  I''ve taken some night shots here as well...   The lighting creates such a brownish yellow cast.  I would prefer this with a little less yellow... maybe desaturate a little in editing.    I also like that you included some of the lighted wall above the top facade.  I never did this in any of my photos.  Overall, great shot, a place I'' enjoy very much!  8 from me.JD Anderson', '2003-08-07 00:52:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(379557, 32027, 10799, '<td valign="top">I like this composition.  The leading lines lead right to the right angle.  Would it have been better to get the right angle a bit more to the side to follow the rule of thirds?</td>', 'I like this composition.  The leading lines lead right to the right angle.  Would it have been better to get the right angle a bit more to the side to follow the rule of thirds?', '2003-08-07 00:52:53.000000', NULL, 1),
