(382569, 31569, 10084, '<td valign="top">Composition is good. Play with f-stop a little bit more. It should give the spider more details.</td>', 'Composition is good. Play with f-stop a little bit more. It should give the spider more details.', '2003-08-09 09:08:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(382570, 32226, 10799, '<td valign="top">I think it would have been a better shot to have the fingers focused.</td>', 'I think it would have been a better shot to have the fingers focused.', '2003-08-09 09:09:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(382572, 31863, 10084, '<td valign="top">If the character is your subject. Play around with your Aperture it will focus in on her. Foreground is blurry and the background is more focus. If background is your subject the girl is in the way. Try moving around the subject and imagine if it would make a good shot. Good thing about digital cameras are you can take multiply shots until you can get it right. <br/>Professionals take hundreds if not thousands of shots to get a few good ones.</td>', 'If the character is your subject. Play around with your Aperture it will focus in on her. Foreground is blurry and the background is more focus. If background is your subject the girl is in the way. Try moving around the subject and imagine if it would make a good shot. Good thing about digital cameras are you can take multiply shots until you can get it right. Professionals take hundreds if not thousands of shots to get a few good ones.', '2003-08-09 09:15:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(382575, 32215, 10084, '<td valign="top">Composition is well done. I like the shadows in the piece. Details in the hands are good. I think the details in the background ruins it a little bit. Maybe if it was a bit blurred out or less detail. A solid color may make a difference</td>', 'Composition is well done. I like the shadows in the piece. Details in the hands are good. I think the details in the background ruins it a little bit. Maybe if it was a bit blurred out or less detail. A solid color may make a difference', '2003-08-09 09:19:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(382578, 31933, 10084, '<td valign="top">A bit of noise. Adjust ISO setting a little. Should improve the red too. Some of the shadows are nice. I think the piece would look better without the frame or at least a black one. It matches the other vertical lines.</td>', 'A bit of noise. Adjust ISO setting a little. Should improve the red too. Some of the shadows are nice. I think the piece would look better without the frame or at least a black one. It matches the other vertical lines.', '2003-08-09 09:22:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(382579, 31480, 10084, '<td valign="top">Washed out picture. Don''t like the colors. You have a really good composition. Playing around more with the setting would make a better photo.</td>', 'Washed out picture. Don''t like the colors. You have a really good composition. Playing around more with the setting would make a better photo.', '2003-08-09 09:26:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(382580, 31520, 2612, '<td valign="top">Your Interpretation of the challenge is good, but I think the focus could be better given the subject was stationary.</td>', 'Your Interpretation of the challenge is good, but I think the focus could be better given the subject was stationary.', '2003-08-09 09:29:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(382582, 32021, 2612, '<td valign="top">Definitely right angles, but the top left seems to be a little out of focus. I know that''s being picky, but I didn''t take much off. I just think still photos of precision instruments usually benefit from sharp focus.</td>', 'Definitely right angles, but the top left seems to be a little out of focus. I know that''s being picky, but I didn''t take much off. I just think still photos of precision instruments usually benefit from sharp focus.', '2003-08-09 09:33:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(382597, 32070, 8274, '<td valign="top">Love the sky, don''t care too much for the silhouette, but that sky gets you marks!</td>', 'Love the sky, don''t care too much for the silhouette, but that sky gets you marks!', '2003-08-09 10:23:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(382604, 32044, 8953, '<td valign="top">We need more like you:) I like your shot. and no question of the angles. you even shot it from an angle. good luck. 9</td>', 'We need more like you:) I like your shot. and no question of the angles. you even shot it from an angle. good luck. 9', '2003-08-09 10:51:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(382606, 32168, 1202, '<td valign="top">Why did you leave the ladder in the shot?  5 with 7 without.</td>', 'Why did you leave the ladder in the shot?  5 with 7 without.', '2003-08-09 11:00:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(382607, 31329, 8953, '<td valign="top">You did a good job of meeting challenge this week:) I wish the image was rotated just about 2 degrees Clockwise, the way it is rotated takes away from the shot for me. otherwise good 5</td>', 'You did a good job of meeting challenge this week:) I wish the image was rotated just about 2 degrees Clockwise, the way it is rotated takes away from the shot for me. otherwise good 5', '2003-08-09 11:00:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(382609, 32075, 8953, '<td valign="top">I love this shot. The colors and texture are wonderful:) You have IMO nailed the challenge. good job. the only problem is I think it is better then mine:) but, alas, truth hurts.......10 from me! good luck</td>', 'I love this shot. The colors and texture are wonderful:) You have IMO nailed the challenge. good job. the only problem is I think it is better then mine:) but, alas, truth hurts.......10 from me! good luck', '2003-08-09 11:04:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(382610, 31771, 8953, '<td valign="top">great shot! meets challenge. the lighting is a bit harsh but overall this works 7</td>', 'great shot! meets challenge. the lighting is a bit harsh but overall this works 7', '2003-08-09 11:05:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(382615, 32042, 1202, '<td valign="top">Interesting picture, are these for growing hops?  8</td>', 'Interesting picture, are these for growing hops?  8', '2003-08-09 11:07:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(382620, 31773, 8953, '<td valign="top">I have left a number of comments this time out, this one begs of it. now I do see angles. and I do see perspective. I like folks that get out of the box. all this gets you  a five, I think the image is a little out of focus and the composition does not have good overall light. I know this will strugle to do well but I wish you luck just the same:) 5</td>', 'I have left a number of comments this time out, this one begs of it. now I do see angles. and I do see perspective. I like folks that get out of the box. all this gets you  a five, I think the image is a little out of focus and the composition does not have good overall light. I know this will strugle to do well but I wish you luck just the same:) 5', '2003-08-09 11:11:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(382623, 32247, 8953, '<td valign="top">overall I like this shot. angles, color, texture and lines bring it together well. the scratches on some of the slate are the only detractors for me. good luck: 8</td>', 'overall I like this shot. angles, color, texture and lines bring it together well. the scratches on some of the slate are the only detractors for me. good luck: 8', '2003-08-09 11:13:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(382624, 31889, 8953, '<td valign="top">through the window shots are not easy to do and this one just did not go well for me. I like that you rotated. a little more contrast and focus. good luck 4</td>', 'through the window shots are not easy to do and this one just did not go well for me. I like that you rotated. a little more contrast and focus. good luck 4', '2003-08-09 11:15:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(382628, 32073, 8953, '<td valign="top">more like...badly broken. good eye though! a little more light and saturation would have worked for me more. 6</td>', 'more like...badly broken. good eye though! a little more light and saturation would have worked for me more. 6', '2003-08-09 11:17:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(382634, 32037, 5822, '<td valign="top">A very compelling image. At first glance, I didn''t like it, and was ready to score it low...but I left it for a while, went to sleep, and came back with a fresh outlook, and now like it very much! It''s grainy appearance works quite well in giving the structure an old, ancient and possibly decaying look that gives the impression of history and antiquity.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I initially felt frustrated at not being able to see the entire structure, but now I like your angle-of-view and the way the right-angle aspect of the challenge comes right "in-your-face" on the left side of the picture giving emphasis to the statue-head.  With the stark grey sky and bird above, there is good balance, and even with a dull and blown out sky, the tonal contrasts between the structure (I''m going to guess it''s a mausoleum) and sky work well. <br/> <br/>The feeling I get from this image is mystical or mythological, as if the bird is an omen to the soothsayers, or prophets, from the gods above (my own whimsical interpretation). I like the way you''ve captured the position of the bird which gives the image a feeling of mystery.  The lighting, while harsh, also adds credence and cohesiveness to the picture giving the impression of  extreme conditions, such as strong winds, emotions, or issues. <br/> <br/>Technically, I think the photo has probably been overly post-processed  (in contrast, brightness and maybe levels) from the original, but makes for a good artistic interpretation on your part.  The B&amp;W rendition is perfect but I would also like to see it monotoned with a very light green or gold. Good job!</td>', 'A very compelling image. At first glance, I didn''t like it, and was ready to score it low...but I left it for a while, went to sleep, and came back with a fresh outlook, and now like it very much! It''s grainy appearance works quite well in giving the structure an old, ancient and possibly decaying look that gives the impression of history and antiquity. Compositionally, I initially felt frustrated at not being able to see the entire structure, but now I like your angle-of-view and the way the right-angle aspect of the challenge comes right "in-your-face" on the left side of the picture giving emphasis to the statue-head.  With the stark grey sky and bird above, there is good balance, and even with a dull and blown out sky, the tonal contrasts between the structure (I''m going to guess it''s a mausoleum) and sky work well.  The feeling I get from this image is mystical or mythological, as if the bird is an omen to the soothsayers, or prophets, from the gods above (my own whimsical interpretation). I like the way you''ve captured the position of the bird which gives the image a feeling of mystery.  The lighting, while harsh, also adds credence and cohesiveness to the picture giving the impression of  extreme conditions, such as strong winds, emotions, or issues.  Technically, I think the photo has probably been overly post-processed  (in contrast, brightness and maybe levels) from the original, but makes for a good artistic interpretation on your part.  The B&W rendition is perfect but I would also like to see it monotoned with a very light green or gold. Good job!', '2003-08-09 11:29:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(382648, 31998, 8891, '<td valign="top">Lovely light on the wood, nice pattern.....HEY YOU KNOW THIS FONT IS BEGINNING TO KILL MY EYES SO I''M GOING TO ALL CAPS.  I''M YELLING NOW BUT WON''T BE AFTER THE 3 DOTS...THERE IS ONE STRAIGHT DUET  OF RAFTERS AND YOU MIGHT HAVE  ROTATED AND CROPPED TO HAVE THAT ONE BIG RIGHT ANGLE IN THIS . ALSO MOVING THE FRAME WHILE SHOOTING....aah heck....the font just sucks period....can they change that? CAN THEY?.....you also might have shot left or right of center to improve the composition.....damn there go my eyes again.....  (sorry about all that....coffee is coming....should help...but nothing is ever going to help this font!)</td>', 'Lovely light on the wood, nice pattern.....HEY YOU KNOW THIS FONT IS BEGINNING TO KILL MY EYES SO I''M GOING TO ALL CAPS.  I''M YELLING NOW BUT WON''T BE AFTER THE 3 DOTS...THERE IS ONE STRAIGHT DUET  OF RAFTERS AND YOU MIGHT HAVE  ROTATED AND CROPPED TO HAVE THAT ONE BIG RIGHT ANGLE IN THIS . ALSO MOVING THE FRAME WHILE SHOOTING....aah heck....the font just sucks period....can they change that? CAN THEY?.....you also might have shot left or right of center to improve the composition.....damn there go my eyes again.....  (sorry about all that....coffee is coming....should help...but nothing is ever going to help this font!)', '2003-08-09 11:59:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(382650, 32127, 8891, '<td valign="top">I like the pano cut but you might have miss calculated on either the amount of BG you used, which provides a nice texture contrasts BTW,  or were not able corp the bottom  and lose the BG there under the corkscrew....troubling...you might have re shot. Cropping that lower right corner out does not kill this.  The strength of the shot should be the right angles of the object not the object itself so you could have gotten away with the crop.</td>', 'I like the pano cut but you might have miss calculated on either the amount of BG you used, which provides a nice texture contrasts BTW,  or were not able corp the bottom  and lose the BG there under the corkscrew....troubling...you might have re shot. Cropping that lower right corner out does not kill this.  The strength of the shot should be the right angles of the object not the object itself so you could have gotten away with the crop.', '2003-08-09 12:04:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(382652, 32029, 8891, '<td valign="top">I like the cross light in this, from the left on the bottom and from the right on top. This produced some fine shadows.  The right angles are missing, however, and I think that might have been either the set up was not purlely right angles or a result of the angle you chose possibly going for the shadow angles which are not right angles either.  I also would have liked to have the center folds straight across the center and not on downward slope. And the lighting on the top might have been less inorder to less the red turning fuschia.  This could be a really fine shot with some changes and I would work on it some more.  Like the idea a lot.</td>', 'I like the cross light in this, from the left on the bottom and from the right on top. This produced some fine shadows.  The right angles are missing, however, and I think that might have been either the set up was not purlely right angles or a result of the angle you chose possibly going for the shadow angles which are not right angles either.  I also would have liked to have the center folds straight across the center and not on downward slope. And the lighting on the top might have been less inorder to less the red turning fuschia.  This could be a really fine shot with some changes and I would work on it some more.  Like the idea a lot.', '2003-08-09 12:10:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(382654, 32196, 8891, '<td valign="top">perfect comp and angles, like the lighting, not a lot of burnout on the gold and the gold brown town  are pleasing as well.</td>', 'perfect comp and angles, like the lighting, not a lot of burnout on the gold and the gold brown town  are pleasing as well.', '2003-08-09 12:11:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(382658, 32191, 8891, '<td valign="top">Very nice,  great angles by the main pole and the  cross bars with lots other angles produce by the ropes (rigging?).  The clouds and sky are wonderful and are a great backgound in this.</td>', 'Very nice,  great angles by the main pole and the  cross bars with lots other angles produce by the ropes (rigging?).  The clouds and sky are wonderful and are a great backgound in this.', '2003-08-09 12:13:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(382660, 32053, 8891, '<td valign="top">The right angles are pure here and I like the black and white on the blue and white. Composition, please....would be better.</td>', 'The right angles are pure here and I like the black and white on the blue and white. Composition, please....would be better.', '2003-08-09 12:15:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(382661, 32021, 8891, '<td valign="top">I think if you had positioned a dark piece or a white piece of paper or material on a diaganol half way under the ruler that this might not have been so dull. Your image might have more tonality in the grayscale but it is too gray throughout here as is (and the white border is not doing it).</td>', 'I think if you had positioned a dark piece or a white piece of paper or material on a diaganol half way under the ruler that this might not have been so dull. Your image might have more tonality in the grayscale but it is too gray throughout here as is (and the white border is not doing it).', '2003-08-09 12:19:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(382667, 32232, 8891, '<td valign="top">I like the steel blue sky behind the sunset lit tree and pole in this. As nice as the tree looks on that sky, and it looks great, the tree totally distracts the pole and the wires. I do not know the set of the surrounds here but you might have shot straight up the pole with you back to it and shot the wires diagonally across the frame.</td>', 'I like the steel blue sky behind the sunset lit tree and pole in this. As nice as the tree looks on that sky, and it looks great, the tree totally distracts the pole and the wires. I do not know the set of the surrounds here but you might have shot straight up the pole with you back to it and shot the wires diagonally across the frame.', '2003-08-09 12:25:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(382669, 31983, 8891, '<td valign="top">Nice abstract, like the textures and colors, looks almost like a Pollock drip splatter detail.</td>', 'Nice abstract, like the textures and colors, looks almost like a Pollock drip splatter detail.', '2003-08-09 12:27:29.000000', NULL, 1);
