(386050, 31570, 9416, '<td valign="top">I was worried that this pic was going to get slammed for the jaggies on the diagonal gutter... <br/>This is my first DPChallenge so thanks for all the feedback on my pic. It was great fun! <br/></td>', 'I was worried that this pic was going to get slammed for the jaggies on the diagonal gutter... This is my first DPChallenge so thanks for all the feedback on my pic. It was great fun! ', '2003-08-13 04:08:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(386056, 31402, 9972, '<td valign="top">Great pic on its own merit. However, in regards to the challenge I personally dont think it fits that well. I was so taken by its eyes I didnt even realise it was in a box at first (I didnt see the title at first either).<br/>FLIP SIDE: I know a good shot when I see it and Im lookin at it. Great to know it was taken with an A70. Dont get discouraged by the blindness and narrowmindedness of voters. Sometimes a shot that doesnt blindingly fit the challenge will excell while other times it will undoubtedly crash and burn. Thats my observation after about a month here.<br/> <br/>Anyway keep up the good work.</td>', 'Great pic on its own merit. However, in regards to the challenge I personally dont think it fits that well. I was so taken by its eyes I didnt even realise it was in a box at first (I didnt see the title at first either).FLIP SIDE: I know a good shot when I see it and Im lookin at it. Great to know it was taken with an A70. Dont get discouraged by the blindness and narrowmindedness of voters. Sometimes a shot that doesnt blindingly fit the challenge will excell while other times it will undoubtedly crash and burn. Thats my observation after about a month here. Anyway keep up the good work.', '2003-08-13 04:20:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(386062, 32201, 10055, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all you had added a comment for my photo. I see some areas where I can work on my skills of taking better photos and what to look for more in a photo.</td>', 'Thank you for all you had added a comment for my photo. I see some areas where I can work on my skills of taking better photos and what to look for more in a photo.', '2003-08-13 04:27:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(386073, 31876, 10739, '<td valign="top">I think many of you have considered this pic completely off-topic and on that basis, it''s been heavily punished on the rates. I don''t like to see pictures that clearly miss the challenge, so I would like to clarify the motivation for this picture in order to judge it in a better way.<br/> <br/>Honestly when I saw the challenge ("right angles to strength the picture"), I thought about the right angle in the sense of "proper" or "correct" angle, not really 90º angle :), in no way... You may think that''s foolish (I do!!), but is the truth and for that reason I thought of a picture in which the strength was coming from using the appropiate angle. In that sense I think the picture was definetely better than the final 3.85 rate. I was surprised that Conceptgraphics got the idea in spite of my missunderstanding, but probably it was hard to realize: I would have thought the pic was out of the challenge too !<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments, I realized my mistake straight away but it was too late :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-13 03:50:10.</i></td>', 'I think many of you have considered this pic completely off-topic and on that basis, it''s been heavily punished on the rates. I don''t like to see pictures that clearly miss the challenge, so I would like to clarify the motivation for this picture in order to judge it in a better way. Honestly when I saw the challenge ("right angles to strength the picture"), I thought about the right angle in the sense of "proper" or "correct" angle, not really 90º angle :), in no way... You may think that''s foolish (I do!!), but is the truth and for that reason I thought of a picture in which the strength was coming from using the appropiate angle. In that sense I think the picture was definetely better than the final 3.85 rate. I was surprised that Conceptgraphics got the idea in spite of my missunderstanding, but probably it was hard to realize: I would have thought the pic was out of the challenge too ! Thanks for the comments, I realized my mistake straight away but it was too late :)', '2003-08-13 04:46:12.000000', '2003-08-13 04:50:10.000000', 0),
(386076, 32053, 8298, '<td valign="top">guess people don''t like centered stock :(</td>', 'guess people don''t like centered stock :(', '2003-08-13 04:51:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(386090, 31615, 6388, '<td valign="top">Very very good shot.  I love the fact that you left he blue in above the window frame.  It adds a whole new element to the pic that would have been lost with a tighter crop.</td>', 'Very very good shot.  I love the fact that you left he blue in above the window frame.  It adds a whole new element to the pic that would have been lost with a tighter crop.', '2003-08-13 05:16:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(386092, 32211, 2780, '<td valign="top">I loved this photo, congrats :)</td>', 'I loved this photo, congrats :)', '2003-08-13 05:18:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(386095, 32075, 6388, '<td valign="top">Glad you weren''t arrested.  You''d best be framing this, David.  I really like the lines in this - challenge aside it''s a great photo with an abstract quality to it.  You''ve a got a great eye.<br/> <br/>Pedro</td>', 'Glad you weren''t arrested.  You''d best be framing this, David.  I really like the lines in this - challenge aside it''s a great photo with an abstract quality to it.  You''ve a got a great eye. Pedro', '2003-08-13 05:20:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(386098, 32073, 6388, '<td valign="top">Great shot Alastair.  I disagree - I think the sky is perfect; sets a definite mood  amongst the other colours.  good work.<br/> <br/>Pedro</td>', 'Great shot Alastair.  I disagree - I think the sky is perfect; sets a definite mood  amongst the other colours.  good work. Pedro', '2003-08-13 05:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(386108, 31913, 6388, '<td valign="top">Either you put some real time into this, or your photoshop skills are getting too good. :) This has a really nice feel to it.  At first glance it seems like a pretty average capture, but there''s lots of hidden gems in it.  good job.</td>', 'Either you put some real time into this, or your photoshop skills are getting too good. :) This has a really nice feel to it.  At first glance it seems like a pretty average capture, but there''s lots of hidden gems in it.  good job.', '2003-08-13 05:32:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(386111, 31615, 6349, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot Nazgul.  Just wanted to welcome you to the 4th place club.  Bet you''re frustrated right now.  I got 4th place on the first photo I ever submitted here.  That was months and months and months and months ago.  I haven''t done better since, still no ribbons for me.  :(  I wish you better luck after your 4th place finish than I had.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Excellent shot Nazgul.  Just wanted to welcome you to the 4th place club.  Bet you''re frustrated right now.  I got 4th place on the first photo I ever submitted here.  That was months and months and months and months ago.  I haven''t done better since, still no ribbons for me.  :(  I wish you better luck after your 4th place finish than I had.  Keep up the good work.', '2003-08-13 05:38:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(386127, 31297, 6349, '<td valign="top">Had to tell you this shot was awesome.  It says New Orleans.  The triangular diagonal composition is perfect with the piano keys and walking feet in the scene.  Very jazzy.  Can''t believe this scored so low.  I guess it was because of the right angle thing, but I think the angles do play a large enough role in the composition for it to be appropriate.  Keep up the excellent work.</td>', 'Had to tell you this shot was awesome.  It says New Orleans.  The triangular diagonal composition is perfect with the piano keys and walking feet in the scene.  Very jazzy.  Can''t believe this scored so low.  I guess it was because of the right angle thing, but I think the angles do play a large enough role in the composition for it to be appropriate.  Keep up the excellent work.', '2003-08-13 06:03:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(386132, 31886, 6349, '<td valign="top">Hey, I thought this was yours cause of the color.  I was right!  Anyway, this image is really nice.  I thought it met the challenge fine.  I''m certainly not blind like the rest of em!  The main flaw I saw in this photo was the compositional placement, which I am sure was intentional, but just bothered my eye a little.  I''m referring to the centeredness of the seats and the horizontal lines in them where the backs are connected and the pillars holding up the roof as contrasted by the position of the seated people.  I feel like my eye is being led on a strange path that is supposed to be straight but isn''t from the bottom center to the top center and then forced to the right.  This power of controlling the eye is a good thing, but in this case the leading lines seem to be drunk.  :)    Well, just my opinion.  Sorry for the long critique.  Hope it''s well taken.  The photo is!  (after careful consideration I place all blame on the person who constructed those bleacher seats.)</td>', 'Hey, I thought this was yours cause of the color.  I was right!  Anyway, this image is really nice.  I thought it met the challenge fine.  I''m certainly not blind like the rest of em!  The main flaw I saw in this photo was the compositional placement, which I am sure was intentional, but just bothered my eye a little.  I''m referring to the centeredness of the seats and the horizontal lines in them where the backs are connected and the pillars holding up the roof as contrasted by the position of the seated people.  I feel like my eye is being led on a strange path that is supposed to be straight but isn''t from the bottom center to the top center and then forced to the right.  This power of controlling the eye is a good thing, but in this case the leading lines seem to be drunk.  :)    Well, just my opinion.  Sorry for the long critique.  Hope it''s well taken.  The photo is!  (after careful consideration I place all blame on the person who constructed those bleacher seats.)', '2003-08-13 06:11:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(386133, 32203, 8643, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a stunning abstract winner.  Please tell us what it is and how you did it!</td>', 'Congratulations on a stunning abstract winner.  Please tell us what it is and how you did it!', '2003-08-13 06:12:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(386135, 31816, 6349, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorite photos of yours yet.  In fact, I am adding it to my favorites.  I would re-voice the opinion that I can''t believe this scored so low, but then again, anything above a 5.5 seems pretty damn good to me these days.  I no longer care about voting either.  In fact, I don''t vote.  I just leave comments on images that impress me, but I wait until after the challenge is over so that I can interpret them with the help of the photographer''s comments.  Keep up the good work and thanks for the recent push to work on my prints for sale and marketing.  I''d be interested to here more about your recent referrer and sales technique if your interesting in sharing.</td>', 'This is one of my favorite photos of yours yet.  In fact, I am adding it to my favorites.  I would re-voice the opinion that I can''t believe this scored so low, but then again, anything above a 5.5 seems pretty damn good to me these days.  I no longer care about voting either.  In fact, I don''t vote.  I just leave comments on images that impress me, but I wait until after the challenge is over so that I can interpret them with the help of the photographer''s comments.  Keep up the good work and thanks for the recent push to work on my prints for sale and marketing.  I''d be interested to here more about your recent referrer and sales technique if your interesting in sharing.', '2003-08-13 06:16:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(386148, 32073, 9886, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone, it''s been a nervous week! Just trying to find out about histogram and soft focus now :).</td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone, it''s been a nervous week! Just trying to find out about histogram and soft focus now :).', '2003-08-13 06:43:45.000000', NULL, 0),
