(386191, 32075, 9885, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot - great use of angles, colour and composition. It''s getting to be a sad world when we can''t even take pictures in a public place without being suspected of nefarious intentions.<br/>Congratulations on your 1st place.<br/>Frank</td>', 'Lovely shot - great use of angles, colour and composition. It''s getting to be a sad world when we can''t even take pictures in a public place without being suspected of nefarious intentions.Congratulations on your 1st place.Frank', '2003-08-13 07:50:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(386193, 32073, 715, '<td valign="top">Hmm, no ribbon:( I''m gonna have my camera for dinner today now.<br/>I agree with Pedro about the sky. I also wanna add, that I really don''t think there is any need for the texture of the tree being visible. The tree''s shape and it''s placement in the landscape are important in this image, not it''s texture.</td>', 'Hmm, no ribbon:( I''m gonna have my camera for dinner today now.I agree with Pedro about the sky. I also wanna add, that I really don''t think there is any need for the texture of the tree being visible. The tree''s shape and it''s placement in the landscape are important in this image, not it''s texture.', '2003-08-13 07:51:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(386198, 32075, 2178, '<td valign="top">Congrats! Very slick, nicely done.</td>', 'Congrats! Very slick, nicely done.', '2003-08-13 07:52:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(386199, 31615, 9913, '<td valign="top">Thanx 4 all the comments :D<br/> <br/>I belive I should have gotten a Ribbon though:o</td>', 'Thanx 4 all the comments :D I belive I should have gotten a Ribbon though:o', '2003-08-13 07:53:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(386204, 32034, 9977, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your usefull comments. As said tarique, he is just cleaning, every contest is a challenge (creativity and imagination). I try to see all around me what can be applied to the theme, sometimes it works, sometimes not. Anyway it is always exciting.<br/>And I will try, thanks to your usefull comments, to do it better.<br/> <br/>Rui Felipe</td>', 'Thank you all for your usefull comments. As said tarique, he is just cleaning, every contest is a challenge (creativity and imagination). I try to see all around me what can be applied to the theme, sometimes it works, sometimes not. Anyway it is always exciting.And I will try, thanks to your usefull comments, to do it better. Rui Felipe', '2003-08-13 08:05:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(386212, 31749, 9889, '<td valign="top">I am one of the three voters who gave a ten to this pic and, of course, I am quite surprised to see that it was not appreciated as it deserved.<br/>Even more surprised that there is people who cannot see the right angle in it...</td>', 'I am one of the three voters who gave a ten to this pic and, of course, I am quite surprised to see that it was not appreciated as it deserved.Even more surprised that there is people who cannot see the right angle in it...', '2003-08-13 08:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(386236, 31841, 10833, '<td valign="top">I''ve been asked why I tilted the picture, so here''s the reason...<br/> <br/>I happened to be driving when I took the shot (partly due to laziness, partly due to the neighborhood :P).  When I looked at the picture, it was tilted.<br/> <br/>I thought really hard about straightening it out, the angle just seemed to kill the symmetry.  Then I thought, "not everything in life is symmetric".<br/> <br/>So, Viola!  The picture kept the tilt that the majority of people really didn''t like :)<br/> <br/>Btw - Thanks, I appreciate the constructive feedback!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-13 07:45:23.</i></td>', 'I''ve been asked why I tilted the picture, so here''s the reason... I happened to be driving when I took the shot (partly due to laziness, partly due to the neighborhood :P).  When I looked at the picture, it was tilted. I thought really hard about straightening it out, the angle just seemed to kill the symmetry.  Then I thought, "not everything in life is symmetric". So, Viola!  The picture kept the tilt that the majority of people really didn''t like :) Btw - Thanks, I appreciate the constructive feedback!', '2003-08-13 08:44:59.000000', '2003-08-13 08:45:23.000000', 0),
(386239, 31773, 9889, '<td valign="top">Firstly, thank you to all commenters.<br/> <br/>My policy and belief are that every comment is helpful.<br/> <br/>Even in this case when the wide majority of comments states (more or less) the same thing: where are the right angles?<br/> <br/>This photo has no evident/visible right angle in the geometric sense.<br/>My interpretation of "right angle" was as the contrary of "wrong angle" and I tought that this pic, in its own way, had a very good "right angle", which is why I posted it.<br/>It would be pedantic to re-cast geometrical right angles in this pic although there are a few subtle ones.<br/> <br/>Of course, I am heart-broken for the performance of this pic.<br/>Particularly because, in the mean time, I got emotively attached to the replicated destiny of its subject. <br/> <br/>My "vengeance" is in posting a pretty boring picture in the next challenge (Desolation), already knowing that it will perform better up to 1 or 2 two points of average, even if it doesn''t have half the strength of this one. Then, after that, I will try to mediate between my true style and what is needed to win a ribbon and I am pretty sure that the result will be quite awful though!!! =)<br/> <br/>I cannot learn from my mistakes if I don''t make them in the first place!<br/> <br/>A very special thanks to those few who, somehow, were striken by this picture as I was: I love you! =)</td>', 'Firstly, thank you to all commenters. My policy and belief are that every comment is helpful. Even in this case when the wide majority of comments states (more or less) the same thing: where are the right angles? This photo has no evident/visible right angle in the geometric sense.My interpretation of "right angle" was as the contrary of "wrong angle" and I tought that this pic, in its own way, had a very good "right angle", which is why I posted it.It would be pedantic to re-cast geometrical right angles in this pic although there are a few subtle ones. Of course, I am heart-broken for the performance of this pic.Particularly because, in the mean time, I got emotively attached to the replicated destiny of its subject.  My "vengeance" is in posting a pretty boring picture in the next challenge (Desolation), already knowing that it will perform better up to 1 or 2 two points of average, even if it doesn''t have half the strength of this one. Then, after that, I will try to mediate between my true style and what is needed to win a ribbon and I am pretty sure that the result will be quite awful though!!! =) I cannot learn from my mistakes if I don''t make them in the first place! A very special thanks to those few who, somehow, were striken by this picture as I was: I love you! =)', '2003-08-13 08:45:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(386331, 32075, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, David!  I love the yellow/orange, it''s beautiful.  How did you get the picture so clear top to bottom, in particular without a tripod?</td>', 'Congratulations, David!  I love the yellow/orange, it''s beautiful.  How did you get the picture so clear top to bottom, in particular without a tripod?', '2003-08-13 10:01:57.000000', NULL, 0),
