(392968, 31650, 6870, '<td valign="top">Hi Christy! Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I concur with all of the compliments below!<br/> <br/>In this shot, i see four children having a good time. Any time you can take a shot of folks having a good time is a worthwhile shot in my book. This shot certainly meets the challenge; right angles are present and easily visible.<br/> <br/>The lighting appears quite bright, yet without harsh shadows, so you must have taken the shot during an overcast sky or perhaps in the shadow of some other building. Taking this shot at the time you did paid off with a pleasant highlight/shadow relationship. One thing to look at here may be your color saturation, or simply making the shot darker to capture some inviting tones. It appears slightly washed out from the greens of the grass to the reds of a couple of the shirts. I''m not sure what post processing software you have, if any, but you might want to revisit this shot and punch some of the colors, lower your levels to take down the highlights just a tad and deepen the shadows--or simply make it darker. It may have been just a little overexposed. That''s my main suggestion for this shot. <br/> <br/>Your composition is good, and I like the high point of view. Someone mentioned the pebbles at lower left, and I suppose they could detract somewhat to some people. Likewise with the curb at upper right.<br/> <br/>What you accomplished here outweighs its weaknesses, though. You''ve captured some kids having a good time, and you met the challenge to boot. The photo exudes joy and happiness and good times. it seems natural, despite the possible call to ''make faces.'' It possesses a sense of whimsy, as you meet the challenge, but in a unique and fun way.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the look!<br/> <br/>If you have questions for me, I''m happy to respond.<br/> <br/>David</td>', 'Hi Christy! Greetings from the Critique Club! I concur with all of the compliments below! In this shot, i see four children having a good time. Any time you can take a shot of folks having a good time is a worthwhile shot in my book. This shot certainly meets the challenge; right angles are present and easily visible. The lighting appears quite bright, yet without harsh shadows, so you must have taken the shot during an overcast sky or perhaps in the shadow of some other building. Taking this shot at the time you did paid off with a pleasant highlight/shadow relationship. One thing to look at here may be your color saturation, or simply making the shot darker to capture some inviting tones. It appears slightly washed out from the greens of the grass to the reds of a couple of the shirts. I''m not sure what post processing software you have, if any, but you might want to revisit this shot and punch some of the colors, lower your levels to take down the highlights just a tad and deepen the shadows--or simply make it darker. It may have been just a little overexposed. That''s my main suggestion for this shot.  Your composition is good, and I like the high point of view. Someone mentioned the pebbles at lower left, and I suppose they could detract somewhat to some people. Likewise with the curb at upper right. What you accomplished here outweighs its weaknesses, though. You''ve captured some kids having a good time, and you met the challenge to boot. The photo exudes joy and happiness and good times. it seems natural, despite the possible call to ''make faces.'' It possesses a sense of whimsy, as you meet the challenge, but in a unique and fun way. Thanks for the look! If you have questions for me, I''m happy to respond. David', '2003-08-19 18:03:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(393205, 31491, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club* <br/> <br/>Your photo is definately of a right angle when you look at it but the landscaping dominates the photo and makes it hard to notice at first.<br/> <br/>You have a very hazy photo which it is likely is a case of weather conditions but you can try correcting it by adjusting the contrast and brightness some as well as more color saturation and you can over come some of the haze.  Also if you are able to set your whitebalance on your camera adjust to to bring out more gold it will overpower the hazy gray and blue tones some.<br/> <br/>It isn''t a bad photo just a little weak for this particular challenge.  Try to brighten it up a little and it will be more appealling.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club*  Your photo is definately of a right angle when you look at it but the landscaping dominates the photo and makes it hard to notice at first. You have a very hazy photo which it is likely is a case of weather conditions but you can try correcting it by adjusting the contrast and brightness some as well as more color saturation and you can over come some of the haze.  Also if you are able to set your whitebalance on your camera adjust to to bring out more gold it will overpower the hazy gray and blue tones some. It isn''t a bad photo just a little weak for this particular challenge.  Try to brighten it up a little and it will be more appealling. Anna', '2003-08-19 21:16:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(393206, 31628, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This is a really nice prespective photo just needs a little more lighting on it to make it really work.  As for meeting the challenge, yes it does there are right angles everywhere. <br/> <br/>It is a refreshing entry.  Very nice perspective.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* This is a really nice prespective photo just needs a little more lighting on it to make it really work.  As for meeting the challenge, yes it does there are right angles everywhere.  It is a refreshing entry.  Very nice perspective. Anna', '2003-08-19 21:19:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(393208, 32235, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I wasn''t sure if I should do this critique but hey if you wanna get mad at me you know where I am...lol<br/> <br/>OK just cause I shot the other side of the hospital did you have to do it directly on?  Seriously yes you met the challenge well this time and yes there are right angles everywhere.  The color is a little off and it is slightly dark near the bottom although I am pretty sure that is cause you took it close to sunset.  Your composition is getting better keep on trying you are getting better.</td>', '*Critique Club* I wasn''t sure if I should do this critique but hey if you wanna get mad at me you know where I am...lol OK just cause I shot the other side of the hospital did you have to do it directly on?  Seriously yes you met the challenge well this time and yes there are right angles everywhere.  The color is a little off and it is slightly dark near the bottom although I am pretty sure that is cause you took it close to sunset.  Your composition is getting better keep on trying you are getting better.', '2003-08-19 21:22:37.000000', NULL, 0),
